{
  "original_id": "newwin-00001-p08",
  "archive_id": "BW2-N01-P08",
  "title": "The NNE distribution on Fuss–Catalan paths with a fixed number of peaks",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every pair of integers m>=2,n>=1 and every integer 1<=k<=n, let W^(m)_(n,k)(t) sum t^nne(D) over all N=(0,1),E=(1,0) paths from (0,0) to (n,mn) whose every prefix satisfies #N>=m#E and which have exactly k consecutive NE factors; nne(D) counts consecutive NNE factors, without cyclic counting. Then W^(m)_(n,k)(t)=(binom(n,k)/n)*sum_{j=1}^k binom(k,j)*binom(mn-k,j-1)*t^j. This polynomial has degree k, a simple root at 0, and k-1 distinct strictly negative roots, so every complex zero is real, proving the complete assertion of source.md.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
